WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.739 --> 00:00:06.580
Have you ever noticed your heart beating faster, your shoulders tightening, or

2
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.404
your stomach feeling unsettled when you’re anxious?

3
00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:13.335
Anxiety can affect both your thoughts and your body.

4
00:00:13.335 --> 00:00:18.103
When your body prepares for a possible threat, you might notice sweating,

5
00:00:18.103 --> 00:00:20.488
tense muscles, or a faster heartbeat.

6
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.688
Those sensations can feel uncomfortable.

7
00:00:23.688 --> 00:00:27.662
But a sensation alone cannot tell you what is causing it.

8
00:00:27.662 --> 00:00:30.770
Physical symptoms can have other causes, too.

9
00:00:31.291 --> 00:00:35.257
Imagine you’re having a busy afternoon and notice tight shoulders.

10
00:00:35.257 --> 00:00:39.343
You might pause, adjust your posture, or take a short break.

11
00:00:39.864 --> 00:00:44.300
If it feels comfortable, notice a neutral point of contact—like your hand

12
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.997
resting on a chair or your feet touching the floor.

13
00:00:48.518 --> 00:00:52.779
If focusing on your body feels unpleasant, look around instead.

14
00:00:52.779 --> 00:00:55.188
Notice the color of a nearby object.

15
00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.751
You can also skip this exercise.

16
00:00:58.273 --> 00:01:01.212
You don’t have to make every sensation disappear.

17
00:01:01.212 --> 00:01:05.722
The aim is to give yourself a moment to notice what’s happening and choose

18
00:01:05.722 --> 00:01:06.688
your next step.

19
00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:12.070
Avoid assuming that a new or concerning symptom is only anxiety.

20
00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:17.912
Seek medical advice when you’re unsure, and urgent medical help for severe or

21
00:01:17.912 --> 00:01:19.261
potentially urgent symptoms.

22
00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:22.565
SteadierMind offers tools for support.

23
00:01:22.565 --> 00:01:25.130
It cannot diagnose physical symptoms.
